// selfhost/codegen/lib.mty
//
// Self-hosted Wasm core-module codegen — v0.13 SHIPPED-SUBSET.
//
// This is the package entry-point for the self-hosted Wasm core-module
// emitter, the last front-end phase to land in Mighty source. It
// documents the intended module layout once cross-file resolution lands;
// today everything is consolidated into `wasm.mty` because the v0.12
// driver still compiles one `.mty` file at a time (see
// `SELFHOST_HIR_V0_8_NOTES.md` gap #1).
//
// ## Intended v1.0+ layout
//
//   selfhost.codegen
//   ├── lib.mty       — this file: re-exports + package decl
//   └── wasm.mty      — MtyIR → Wasm core-module emitter (runnable,
//                       v0.13 subset)
//
// ## Current v0.13 layout (single-file compile workaround)
//
// The runnable emitter + bridge live in `wasm.mty`. `lib.mty` exists
// for parity with the `selfhost/ir` layout and to provide a single
// package id (`selfhost_codegen`) for downstream importers.
//
// ## Status
//
// - `wasm.mty` — `mty check` clean, services the v0.13 bootstrap test
//
// ## Why ship a SUBSET
//
// The Rust Wasm core-module lowerer in `crates/mty-codegen-wasm/src/emit.rs`
// is ~1700 LOC and exercises the entirety of the `wasm-encoder`
// section/instruction API. The v0.13 self-host budget is 5 hours and the
// language-level byte-manipulation primitives Mighty would need to write
// real LEB128 / canonical-ABI byte emitters are NOT yet in the stdlib
// (Vec[U8], for-each-byte, bitwise shifts on byte streams). The Mighty
// emitter therefore drives **section-level + instruction-level Wasm
// shape decisions** via a host-bridge event stream — exactly the same
// architectural choice the lexer (v0.4-v0.5), parser (v0.6),
// HIR (v0.8), typeck (v0.8), and MtyIR (v0.9) phases made.
//
// The actual byte serialization (LEB128 encoding, magic header, version
// bytes, etc.) is done by the trusted Rust `wasm-encoder` crate in the
// bootstrap test host. The Mighty source is responsible for:
//
//   1. Selecting which Wasm sections are needed (type / function /
//      export / code).
//   2. Computing the function type signature (params, results) for
//      each MtyIR fn.
//   3. Walking each MtyIR block + statement + rvalue + terminator
//      and emitting the corresponding Wasm opcode marker.
//   4. Recording local variable slots for `local.get`/`local.set`.
//   5. Closing each function body with the right `end` markers.
//
// After the bootstrap test runs the Mighty emitter, the host reassembles
// a real Wasm core module from the event stream and validates it with
// `wasmparser::Validator::validate_all` — the same correctness check
// the trusted Rust codegen pipeline uses in
// `crates/mty-driver/tests/conformance_codegen.rs`.
//
// See `crates/mty-driver/tests/selfhost_codegen.rs` for the runner
// and `dev/history/notes/SELFHOST_CODEGEN_V0_13_NOTES.md` for the
// production matrix + gap catalog.

package selfhost_codegen
